CRASH-09: skip the transfer of plowed snow when no receiving subcatchment is named

The receiving subcatchment is the optional last field of a [SNOWPACKS]
REMOVAL line; when it is left out, toSubcatch is -1. snow_plowSnow() then
read Subcatch[-1].snowpack whenever Fsub > 0 (heap out-of-bounds read, and
a write through the pointer it finds). Only transfer snow when a
subcatchment was named. The Fsub share then stays on the plowable area, as
it already does when the receiving subcatchment has no pervious snow area,
and as 6.0.0's SnowSolver::plowSnow() does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-09_swmm530.patch

